    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Jousting in January is a <span class=\"bb_strike\">goofy side project thrown together to pass the time while working on Parkour Posse</span> free for all arcade game in which you must strike the enemy before they get you. 1 hit kill. 1st hit wins. Game features include: </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- 8 levels randomly selected at the start of each round</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- 2+ players in local multiplayer</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- An easy access Quit Game button so you can go run conveniently timed errands before your friends catch up to your score</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Melee weapon that can be thrown as a projectile (or left on the ground like a spike trap in one of those dimly lit parts of the map)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Movement in 8 directions</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >P.S. You will be unarmed after throwing your lance. You'll have to go pick it up or lead the enemies to your lance sitting on the ground.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Jousting in January is a <span class=\"bb_strike\">goofy side project thrown together to pass the time while working on Parkour Posse</span> free for all arcade game in which you must strike the enemy before they get you. 1 hit kill. 1st hit wins. Game features include: </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- 8 levels randomly selected at the start of each round</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- 2+ players in local multiplayer</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- An easy access Quit Game button so you can go run conveniently timed errands before your friends catch up to your score</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Melee weapon that can be thrown as a projectile (or left on the ground like a spike trap in one of those dimly lit parts of the map)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Movement in 8 directions</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >P.S. You will be unarmed after throwing your lance. You'll have to go pick it up or lead the enemies to your lance sitting on the ground.</p>",
    "short_description": "Murderize your enemy(ies). No retreat. No surrender.",
